    "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1288?c=uis": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (up to 3 positions)",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (up to 3 positions) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (up to 3 positions) Springfield, IL, United States | 1005089 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/3/2026 Back to Search Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (up to 3 positions) Posting Category: The University of Illinois Springfield invites applications for three inaugural faculty positions (preferred start date January 1, 2027; latest start August 16, 2027) in Engineering Technology to launch the Bachelor of Applied Science in Engineering Technology (BAS-ET), beginning Fall 2027. These positions will form the founding faculty cohort and will collectively deliver the core curriculum, establish the work-based learning sequence with regional employers, and prepare for ABET ETAC accreditation. We are seeking candidates whose expertise spans applied engineering technology. The final composition of the cohort will be shaped by the strength of the applicant pool, with the goal of assembling a team that collectively covers the program's instructional needs. Preferred areas of expertise include automation, robotics, and industrial controls; engineering design, CAD/CAM, and manufacturing systems; systems integration, project management, and applied engineering practice; materials, measurement, and quality systems; and work-based learning coordination and industry partnership development. Significant industry experience is strongly preferred. A mix of tenure-track and non-tenure track hires is anticipated. View the tenure-track job posting at: https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1287?c=uis These are full-time on-campus and benefit-eligible non-tenured academic appointments. UIS faculty are expected to be available and engaged in the university community to perform professional responsibilities as assigned. Responsibilities: Teaching: Faculty will deliver core coursework in the Bachelor of Applied Science in Engineering Technology. Teaching assignments will be determined based on each faculty member's expertise and the collective needs of the founding cohort . Service: All faculty are expected to contribute to the development and growth of the BAS-ET program and the School of Applied Engineering through active participation in program-level, college-level, and university service. Service responsibilities include participation in the program's industry advisory board, including development and maintenance of employer relationships for work-based learning placements; community college partnership development, including articulation agreement planning and transfer pathway coordination; ABET ETAC accreditation preparation, self-study documentation, and continuous improvement processes; K-12 pipeline engagement, including support for the techX dual-credit program at the Capital Area Career Center; student recruitment activities, including prospective student outreach, campus visit participation, and community college advising events; and standard college and university committee service as assigned. In the program's early years, service will be weighted toward accreditation preparation and partnership development. As the program matures, faculty service responsibilities will normalize to reflect the standard expectations across the college.college and university committee service as assigned. Visa sponsorship is not available for these positions Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in engineering, engineering technology, engineering education, manufacturing, applied science, or a closely related STEM discipline Minimum five years of substantial professional industry experience in an engineering or technical leadership role Demonstrated ability or potential to teach in applied, hands-on, lab-intensive learning environments Commitment to work-based learning and employer-integrated education Preferred Qualifications : Experience with ABET-accredited programs or accreditation processes\nExperience with community college transfer student populations\nExperience designing or coordinating cooperative education, internship, or work-based learning programs\nExpertise in one or more: automation, robotics, and industrial controls; engineering design, CAD/CAM, and manufacturing systems; systems integration and project management; materials, measurement, and quality systems Application deadline (5pm): 10/19/2026 Nine-month salary: $110-130,000 Application instructions: Click the \"Apply Now\" button, create or update your profile, complete the online application, and upload 1) cover letter addressing the required and preferred qualifications, including which of the program's instructional areas the candidate is prepared to teach and your interest in a founding-faculty role, 2) curriculum vitae or resume, including professional industry experience,  3) statement of teaching philosophy, addressing applied, hands-on, lab-intensive instruction and experience with student populations such as transfer students and working adults, and 4) a statement of professional practice. Contact information for professional references will be requested later in the search process. Formal review of applications will begin soon after the application deadline and continue until the position is filled or the search is terminated. About UIS: Located in the state \ncapital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members \nof the University of Illinois system. The University serves \napproximately 4,000 students in 60 undergraduate programs of study, 41 \nminors, 44 graduate programs of study, 1 doctorate, 43 graduate \ncertificates, and coursework that leads to 8 ISBE endorsements. The \nacademic curriculum offers students a strong liberal arts core, a wide \nrange of professional programs, and close faculty interaction. Making \nthe most of its location in the state capital, UIS is broadly engaged in\n public policy and service. Its diverse student body includes \ntraditional, non-traditional, and international students. Twenty-five \npercent of majors are in 17 undergraduate and graduate online degree \nprograms and the campus has received several national awards for its \nimplementation of online learning. UIS faculty are committed teachers, \nactive scholars, and professionals in service to society. The University\n emphasizes excellence in teaching, and faculty are also expected to \nprovide a balance of scholarship and service activities to meet \nrequirements for tenure and promotion. You are encouraged to visit the \nuniversity web page at https://www.uis.edu and the college web page at https://www.uis.edu/chst. About Springfield, Illinois: https://www.uis.edu/academic-affairs/about-our-springfield-community Union Affiliation: This position is included in a bargaining unit (UPI Local 4100 UIS Nontenure-Track Faculty Union). This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State University Retirement System. You will not pay Social Security taxes and your earning will not be on your Social Security Record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages. Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"
