    "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1287?c=uis": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (3 positions)",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (3 positions) Springfield, IL, United States | 1005088 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/3/2026 Back to Search Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (3 positions) | Job Details Assistant or Associate Professor, Engineering Technology (3 positions) Posting Category: Summary: The University of Illinois Springfield invites applications for up to three inaugural tenure-track faculty positions (Assistant or Associate Professor, preferred start date January 1, 2027 and latest start date August 16, 2027) in Engineering Technology to launch the Bachelor of Applied Science in Engineering Technology (BAS-ET), beginning Fall 2027. These positions will form the founding faculty cohort and will collectively deliver the core curriculum, establish the work-based learning sequence with regional employers, and prepare for ABET ETAC accreditation. We are seeking candidates whose expertise spans applied engineering technology. The final composition of the cohort will be shaped by the strength of the applicant pool, with the goal of assembling a team that collectively covers the program's instructional needs. Preferred areas of expertise include automation, robotics, and industrial controls; engineering design, CAD/CAM, and manufacturing systems; systems integration, project management, and applied engineering practice; materials, measurement, and quality systems; and work-based learning coordination and industry partnership development. Significant industry experience is strongly preferred. These are full-time on-campus tenure-track academic appointments. UIS tenure-system faculty are expected to be available and engaged in the university community, with assigned professional responsibilities for teaching, scholarship, and service. A mix of tenure-system and non-tenure system faculty may comprise this cohort. View the clinical faculty posting: https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1288?c=uis Visa sponsorship is not available for these positions. Duties & Responsibilities: Teaching: Faculty will deliver core coursework in the Bachelor of Applied Science in Engineering Technology. Teaching assignments will be determined based on each faculty member's expertise and the collective needs of the founding cohort. Scholarship: Faculty are expected to develop an active program of applied research or scholarly activity appropriate to the discipline of engineering technology. This may include industry-sponsored applied research projects with regional partners; design, development, and evaluation of work-based learning pedagogy and assessment models; scholarship of teaching and learning in engineering technology education; workforce development research in collaboration with employer and community college partners; and contributions to professional societies such as ASEE or ABET. Given the applied nature of the program, scholarship that bridges academic inquiry and industry practice is especially valued. The expectation is that scholarly activity will be productive and sustained, consistent with the standards for tenure and promotion at UIS, while recognizing that the early years of a new program will require significant effort in curriculum development, accreditation preparation, and partnership building. Service: All faculty are expected to contribute to the development and growth of the BAS-ET program and the School of Applied Engineering through active participation in program-level, college-level, and university service. Service responsibilities include participation in the program's industry advisory board, including development and maintenance of employer relationships for work-based learning placements; community college partnership development, including articulation agreement planning and transfer pathway coordination; ABET ETAC accreditation preparation, self-study documentation, and continuous improvement processes; K-12 pipeline engagement, including support for the techX dual-credit program at the Capital Area Career Center; student recruitment activities, including prospective student outreach, campus visit participation, and community college advising events; and standard college and university committee service as assigned. In the program's early years, service will be weighted toward accreditation preparation and partnership development. As the program matures, faculty service responsibilities will normalize to reflect the standard expectations across the college.college and university committee service as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree in engineering, engineering technology, engineering education, manufacturing, applied science, or a closely related STEM discipline (ABD considered with expected completion within one year of start date) Professional experience in an engineering, manufacturing, automation, construction, infrastructure, or related technical industry Demonstrated ability or potential to teach in applied, hands-on, lab-intensive learning environments Record of or clear potential for applied research, scholarship, or creative activity appropriate to rank Commitment to work-based learning and employer-integrated education Preferred Qualifications: Experience with ABET-accredited programs or accreditation processes Experience with community college transfer student populations Experience designing or coordinating cooperative education, internship, or work-based learning programs Record of industry-sponsored projects, applied research, or scholarship of teaching and learning Expertise in one or more: automation, robotics, and industrial controls; engineering design, CAD/CAM, and manufacturing systems; systems integration and project management; materials, measurement, and quality systems Application deadline: 10/19/2026 Nine-month salary: $110-130,000 Application instructions: Click the \"Apply Now\" button at the top or bottom of the posting, create or update your profile, complete the \nonline application, and upload 1) cover letter addressing\n     the required and preferred qualifications, including which of the\n     program's instructional areas the candidate is prepared to teach and their\n     interest in a founding-faculty role, 2) curriculum vitae or\n     resume, including professional industry experience, 3) statement of teaching philosophy, addressing applied, hands-on, lab-intensive instruction and experience with student populations such as transfer students and working adults, 4) statement of applied research/scholarship interests, and 5) unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire).\n. Contact information for professional references will be requested later in the search process. Formal review \nof applications will begin soon after application deadline and continue until the position is filled or the search is terminated. About\nUIS: Located in the state capital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members of the University of Illinois system. The University serves approximately 4,000 students in 60 undergraduate \nprograms of study, 41 minors, 44 graduate programs of study, 1 doctorate, 43 graduate certificates, coursework that leads to 8 ISBE endorsements. The academic curriculum offers students a strong liberal \narts core, a wide range of professional programs, and close faculty interaction. Making the most of its location in the state capital, UIS is broadly engaged in public policy and service. Its diverse \nstudent body includes traditional, non-traditional, and international students. Twenty-five percent of majors are in 17 undergraduate and graduate online degree programs and the campus has received \nseveral national awards for its implementation of online learning. UIS faculty are committed teachers, active scholars, and professionals in service to society. The University emphasizes excellence in \nteaching, and faculty are also expected to provide a balance of scholarship and service activities to meet requirements for tenure and promotion. You are encouraged to visit the university web page at https://www.uis.edu and the college web page at: https://www.uis.edu/chst About Springfield, Illinois: https://www.uis.edu/academic-affairs/about-our-springfield-community/ Union Affiliation: Tenure-track faculty positions at more than half-time are represented by the University Professionals of Illinois (UPI) Local 4100, University of Illinois Springfield United Faculty Chapter, IFT-AFT, AFL-CIO. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic information, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment . As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility . The University of Illinois offers a very competitive benefits portfolio. Click for a complete list of Employee Benefits. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State Universities Retirement System You do not pay Social Security taxes and your earnings will not be on your Social Security record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages.) Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Requests may be submitted by contacting UIS HR at hremployment@uis.edu or call 217-206-6652. ***Please Note: All postings close at 5:00pm CST on the posting close date.*** Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"
    },
    "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/868?c=uis": {
      "title": "Extra Help Event Attendant - 50 Vacancies",
      "description": "Extra Help Event Attendant - 50 Vacancies | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Extra Help Event Attendant - 50 Vacancies Springfield, IL, United States | 1004083 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 5/27/2026 Back to Search Extra Help Event Attendant - 50 Vacancies Posting Category: About UIS: Located in the state capital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members of the University of Illinois system. The University serves more than 4,000 students in 44 graduate and 56 undergraduate programs. You are encouraged to visit the university web page at http://www.uis.edu . Application deadline: Open Until Filled Hourly Rate: $20.00 Summary: Extra Help Event Attendants provide event related services in a variety of different areas of operations including: concession stand, merchandise sales, artist runner and access control. Duties & Responsibilities: Parking Attendant (Non-Driving): Assist in setting up traffic cones and signs for event parking and VIP parking. Provide general patron assistance and directions into the building and to events. Monitor parking lot for available parking spaces. Assist in tearing down traffic cones and signs at the end of the shift. Provide patron assistance exiting the building, to cars, and exiting the University. Concession Stand Attendant (Non-Alcohol): Serve as the primary point of contact for customer service and sales at events. Prepare the concession stand for sales, ensuring all areas are clean and stocked. Operate point of sale systems, cash drawers, and credit card machines. Take orders for beverages and food items, finalize sales, and restock products. Shut down and reconcile point of sale systems and cash drawers. Clean all machines, countertops, and other work areas. Ensure the concession stand is ready for the next use. Merchandise Seller: Act as the PAS representative in fulfilling artist merchandise sales. Work with artist’s representative to prepare and sell merchandise. Operate point of sale systems, cash drawers, and credit card machines. Assist with finalizing product counts and shutting down merchandise areas. Clean all work areas. Artist Attendant (Non-Driving): Assist in fulfilling the needs of the artists and their traveling staff. Prepare and monitor hospitality rooms, stock supplies, and clean hospitality areas. Monitor access control at backstage doors and other specified areas. Artist Runner/Attendant (Driving): Fulfill all duties of the Artist Attendant role. Run errands and fulfill hospitality contracts. Drive members of the artist’s team locally (vehicle provided by the university). Access Control Attendant: Ensure patrons, artists, and staff follow policies and procedures for accessing event areas. Place signage and access control features, scan tickets, review credentials, and inspect packages. Guide patrons through metal detectors and request UIS Police assistance if necessary. Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma, some college preferred. Age requirement: 18 years old minimum for all positions OR 21 years old for driving positions as indicated above. UIS background check – must pass prior to starting work. AED (Automated External Defibrillator) training (provided). Cash handling and credit card training for applicable positions (provided). Applicants must be able to provide exceptional customer service to diverse groups of people including: the public, students, event promoters, and University department representatives. Must have a positive friendly attitude, be clean and well-groomed, possess good interpersonal communication skills, and remain calm while managing a life safety evacuation or other emergency. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Standing for long periods of time. Occasional lifting, up to 30 lbs. Physical Demands: Standing : Frequently Walking : Frequently Sitting : Rarely Lifting : Frequently Carrying : Frequently Pushing : Frequently Pulling : Frequently Climbing : Rarely Balancing : Rarely Stooping : Occasionally Kneeling : Occasionally Crouching : Occasionally Crawling : Rarely Reaching : Occasionally Handling : Frequently Grasping : Frequently Feeling : Occasionally Talking : Frequently Hearing : Frequently Repetitive Motions : Frequently Eye/Hand/Foot Coordination : Frequently Taste/Smell : Rarely Performing Manual Tasks : Frequently Employment Policies and other information: The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence,\nequity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic\ninformation, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility This position is not eligible for benefits. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State Universities Retirement System You do not pay Social Security taxes and your earnings will not be on your Social Security record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages.) Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"
