    "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1320?c=uis": {
      "title": "Executive Director, Innovation and Opportunity",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Executive Director, Innovation and Opportunity Springfield, IL, United States | 1005151 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/1/2026 Back to Search Executive Director, Innovation and Opportunity | Job Details Executive Director, Innovation and Opportunity Posting Category: E About UIS: Located in the state capital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members of the University of Illinois system. The University serves more than 4,000 students in 44 graduate and 56 undergraduate programs.  You are encouraged to visit the university web page at http://www.uis.edu . Application deadline: Open Until Filled Please apply by September 18, 2026 for priority consideration. Proposed Annual Salary: $120,000 Summary: The Executive Director of Innovation and Opportunity (ED) at the University of Illinois Springfield will lead innovation and economic development efforts at UIS to benefit the regional economy in collaboration with local industry, government partners, Continuing and Professional Education (CAPE), and the Illinois Innovation Network (IIN). These efforts will be primarily conducted through the development and execution of related programming at Innovate Springfield, UIS' downtown Springfield innovation center and founding hub of the IIN. The Executive Director (ED) will lead Innovate Springfield's strategic framework across five interconnected pillars: business incubation and venture growth; business modernization and applied innovation; CAPE-delivered professional education and workforce development; student talent pipeline and engagement; and emerging technology awareness. Working closely with UIS leaders, faculty, staff, students, and community partners, the ED will develop and implement entrepreneurial and applied innovation initiatives that advance these strategic priorities. These activities will accelerate regional technology adoption, foster interdisciplinary collaboration, strengthen educational opportunities, inform public policy, and promote social innovation throughout the region. Duties & Responsibilities: Innovate Springfield Strategy and Governance. Work with internal and external partners to resource, develop, direct and implement all Innovate Springfield strategies aligned with UIS’ strategic priorities and the Innovate Springfield strategic framework, and ensure the successful execution of Innovate Springfield operations and UIS innovation and economic development activities in collaboration with other program leads. Staff and lead advisory boards and related committees, ensuring regional input is translated into UIS programs, partnerships and measurable outcomes. Lead all aspects of programming across Innovate Springfield’s five pillars — business incubation and acceleration, business modernization and applied innovation, professional education and workforce development, student talent pipeline, and emerging-technology awareness. Financial Sustainability. Develop, lead and ensure financial support and viability of Innovate Springfield’s operations, as well as the business incubation and acceleration programs and Innovate Springfields’s partnership model with Continuing and Professional Education (CAPE) for scalable, credential-generating programming. Develop, implement, and manage Innovate Springfield's operations and budget to ensure efficient service delivery and long-term financial sustainability. Collaborate with UIS Advancement and program leaders to secure financial support for Innovate Springfield's operations and programs. Establish and monitor meaningful performance measures, including a quarterly outcomes dashboard, to evaluate progress and organizational success. Programming Effectiveness. Ensure effectiveness across all Innovate Springfield programs — including business modernization and applied innovation (such as a recurring AI-adoption demonstration series and the region’s AI community of practice), CAPE-delivered professional education and stackable credentials, and emerging-technology awareness — by working with other UIS leaders responsible for programing in such areas as technology and research commercialization, social innovation, public policy, and experiential and workforce education, as well as other program areas determined by the UIS Chancellor. Regional Partnerships. Develop and coordinate all UIS’ initiatives with other UIS leaders responsible for programing to bring innovation to bear on the broad range of community and regional needs and problems. Actively engage current and potential partners in business, finance, government, healthcare, insurance, manufacturing, philanthropy, and scientific communities, as well as academic partners across the IIN, to invest in and advance an entrepreneurial and technology-adoption culture within and beyond UIS to strengthen economic development and innovation in the Springfield region. Academic and Student Engagement. Work with academic units — including the College of Business and Management, the College of Health, Science and Technology, and CAPE — to develop high-impact, applied learning opportunities for students related to innovation, entrepreneurship, and business modernization, and to connect youth and workforce programming to UIS degree and certificate pathways, with relevance to local economic and community development. Serve as UIS representative on IIN Council and various UI System committees. Staff Supervision. Supervise and oversee Innovate Springfield staff, as well as participating business incubation and CAPE program partners, for Innovate Springfield programing and operational success. Provide effective leadership, direction and support for staff to be successful at their assigned duties. Give staff frequent performance feedback and support their professional development. Visibility and Reporting. Develop and implement strategies, including regular dashboard reporting to the Advisory Board and UIS leadership, to highlight the value and successes of UIS’ innovative and economic development activities in order to enhance Innovate Springfield visibility and reputation with internal and external stakeholders, including UIS leaders, faculty, students, business leaders, public officials and IIN partners. Advisory Role. Advise the Chancellor on economic development, innovation, and emerging-technology issues, and participate in committees, working groups, etc., as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree from an accredited institution (in some cases, extensive work experience in innovation, incubation and/or economic development fields could replace a master’s degree requirement; in such cases, a bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution is required) A strong track record of leading innovation and entrepreneurship ecosystems and programs, including experience at innovation centers and/or business incubators ●\tStrong background in business commercialization, community and regional economic development, and social innovation ●\tExperience and deep knowledge of the requisites of the business startup process, including business planning, operations, financing and insight into local economic and social conditions ●\tSupervisory experience Preferred Qualifications: Advanced degree from an accredited institution Experience working with faculty, staff and senior academic leadership at a higher education institution Investment and commercialization expertise; ability to identify, evaluate and effectuate investments Technical skill in projecting the economic and social impact of new and developing businesses and initiatives Experience with business incubation and acceleration Experience with business modernization, applied AI, or data-driven technology-adoption programming Experience partnering with professional/continuing education units to convert applied programming into scalable credentials and workforce training Familiarity with emerging technologies (e.g., artificial intelligence, data analytics, cybersecurity) and their translation into accessible public programming Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Demonstrated passion for innovation in general and for bringing ideas to market Demonstrated success establishing and maintaining relationships across a variety of networks, such as in higher education, business sectors, venture investing, nonprofits, and/or community organizations Success leading large teams, administrating committees and supervising employees High level of integrity and exceptional interpersonal and team-building skills Excellent written and oral communication skills Cultural competency to work with diverse groups and build an inclusive work environment Willingness to accommodate meetings/activities outside normal business hours Passion for advancing communities through innovation, business development and building capacity for social impact endeavors Ability to translate regional technology trends and employer needs into applied programming, professional education, and academic partnerships Knowledge of applied AI, data analytics, and emerging-technology trends relevant to business, government, and healthcare sectors Employment Policies and other information: The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic information, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment . As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility . This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State University Retirement System. You will not pay Social Security taxes and your earning will not be on your Social Security Record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages. Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Requests may be submitted by contacting UIS HR at hremployment@uis.edu or call 217-206-6652. ***Please Note: All postings close at 5:00pm CST on the posting close date.*** Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"
    },
    "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1307?c=uis": {
      "title": "Admission Counselor (Campus Based)-Two Vacancies",
      "description": "Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Admission Counselor (Campus Based)-Two Vacancies Springfield, IL, United States | 1005137 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/13/2026 Back to Search Admission Counselor (Campus Based)-Two Vacancies | Job Details Admission Counselor (Campus Based)-Two Vacancies Posting Category: E About UIS: Located in the state capital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members of the University of Illinois system. The University serves more than 4,000 students in 44 graduate and 56 undergraduate programs.  You are encouraged to visit the university web page at http://www.uis.edu . Application deadline: Open Until Filled Minimum Starting Salary: $44,000.00 annually Summary: The admissions counselor position is responsible for recruiting and supporting new students at University of Illinois Springfield. This position represents the University at on- and off-campus events, including college fairs, school visits, daily campus visits, and large admissions programs. Counselors serve as key points of contact for school counselors, students, and families, providing guidance throughout the college search, admission, and enrollment process. The position requires strong communication and interpersonal skills to engage effectively with students, families, faculty, staff, and advisors. Responsibilities include delivering presentations to groups of varying sizes, conducting one-on-one meetings, and assisting with inquiries to ensure a positive experience for prospective students. This role plays a central part in shaping the first impressions of University of Illinois Springfield while supporting its enrollment goals through strategic outreach and personalized student support. Duties & Responsibilities: Outreach: 1. Attend school visits, college fairs, conferences, open houses, and other specialty events presenting to attendees. 2. Craft and execute targeted outreach plans in line with the enrollment strategy.\n3. Conduct webinars to increase knowledge of UIS as needed.\n4. Provide presentations to prospective students and families and provide tours as needed for prospective students and families. Recruitment: 1. Identifies, recruits and enrolls prospective undergraduate and graduate students within an assigned territory. 2. Develops and maintains relationships with prospective students and their support systems from the inquiry stage throughout the admissions funnel utilizing various communication tactics and platforms, including phone calls, video conferencing, and written correspondence. 3. Craft and execute targeted recruitment plans in line with the enrollment strategy. Application Review: Read and evaluate admissions applications, using a holistic view of each applicant to make decisions that align with our campus's enrollment targets. Partnership Outreach - Develops and maintains relationships with high school counselors, community college advisors, and college career counselors, providing timely updates and support for them and their students. Other: 1. Assist with admissions operational functions. 2. Engage in developing and executing communication campaigns, search committees, and various on-campus initiatives.  3. Actively participate and contribute to relevant professional organizations.\n4. Join various admissions-related projects and tasks as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: 1. Bachelor’s degree 2. Valid driver’s license 3. Ability to present to both large and small groups 4. Ability to work independently and cooperatively with external and internal partners 5. Excellent oral and written communication skills 6. Excellent organizational and time management skills 7.Proficiency in general office software, such as word processing, spreadsheets, email, etc 8. Ability to travel overnight and work a flexible schedule including some early mornings, late evenings, and weekends when required. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Experience presenting to audiences 2. Experience with Technolutions Slate CRM 3. Bilingual Spanish/English. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Ability to work independently and collaboratively Excellent oral and written communication skills Excellent organizational and time management skills Proficiency in general office software, such as word processing, spreadsheets, email, etc Ability to travel overnight and work a flexible schedule including some evenings and weekends when required. Required abilities include speaking and hearing for in-person and virtual communication, using close and distance vision when reading documents or viewing screens, and performing tasks with repetitive fine motor skills. Physical Demands: Standing : Occasionally Walking : Occasionally Sitting : Frequently Lifting : Occasionally Carrying : Occasionally Pushing : Occasionally Pulling : Occasionally Climbing : Rarely Balancing : Rarely Stooping : Occasionally Kneeling : Rarely Crouching : Occasionally Crawling : Rarely Reaching : Occasionally Handling : Occasionally Grasping : Rarely Feeling : Rarely Talking : Constantly Hearing : Constantly Repetitive Motions : Rarely Eye/Hand/Foot Coordination : Rarely Taste/Smell : Rarely Performing Manual Tasks : Rarely Working Conditions: Extreme cold : Occasionally Extreme heat : Occasionally Humid : Occasionally Wet : Occasionally Noise : Constantly Hazards : Rarely Temperature Change : Rarely Atmospheric Conditions : Rarely Vibration : Rarely Travel Requirements: 40% Recruitment Travel Employment Policies and other information: The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic information, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment . As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility . This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State University Retirement System. You will not pay Social Security taxes and your earning will not be on your Social Security Record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages. Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Requests may be submitted by contacting UIS HR at hremployment@uis.edu or call 217-206-6652. ***Please Note: All postings close at 5:00pm CST on the posting close date.*** Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"
