    "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1350?c=uis": {
      "title": "Extra Help Athletics Communication Assistant",
      "description": "Extra Help Athletics Communication Assistant | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Extra Help Athletics Communication Assistant Springfield, IL, United States | 1005202 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/22/2026 Back to Search Extra Help Athletics Communication Assistant Posting Category: About UIS: Located in the state capital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members of the University of Illinois system. The University serves more than 4,000 students in 44 graduate and 56 undergraduate programs. You are encouraged to visit the university web page at http://www.uis.edu . Application deadline: 11/5/2026 Minimum Starting Salary: $20 per hour Summary: The Athletics Communications Assistant will support the day-to-day communications operations of UIS Athletics through in-game coverage, written content, feature storytelling, digital content and athletics communications support. Working closely with the Assistant AD for Strategic Communication and Operations, this position will help provide timely and accurate coverage of Prairie Stars teams and student-athletes while supporting the department's broader communications efforts.\nThis position is designed to provide immediate additional capacity within the Athletics Communications office. The assistant will have opportunities to work across multiple sports and communications functions, gaining hands-on experience while contributing directly to the department's daily operations. Duties & Responsibilities: Game and Event Coverage - Assist with in-game communications coverage for UIS athletic events, including live updates, scoring information, statistics, social media content and other game-day communications needs. Attend athletic events as assigned to provide timely coverage and collect content for use across UIS Athletics digital platforms. Assist with gathering photos, video, quotes, notes and other information needed for postgame coverage and digital content. Support game-day communications operations, including coordination with coaches, student-athletes, officials, event staff and other athletics personnel. Assist with coverage of home and away events based on departmental needs. Writing and Editorial Content - Write game recaps, previews, feature stories, releases and other athletics-related content. Assist with researching, interviewing and developing feature stories highlighting UIS student-athletes, coaches, teams and programs. Gather information from coaches, student-athletes and staff to support accurate and timely storytelling. Proofread and edit athletics communications materials for accuracy, clarity, AP style and consistency with UIS Athletics standards. Assist with maintaining timely postgame and post-event coverage across assigned sports. Digital and Social Media Content - Assist with creating and publishing social media content during and around athletic events. Develop short-form written content, game updates, highlights and other material for UIS Athletics social media platforms. Help identify opportunities to capture content that can be used across multiple communications platforms. Assist with maintaining consistent messaging and branding across athletics digital channels. Communications Operations and Processes -Assist the Assistant AD for Strategic Communication and Operations with daily athletics communications responsibilities and departmental projects. Support the development, organization and improvement of communications processes, workflows and resources. Assist with maintaining records, historical information, statistics, rosters and other materials used in athletics communications. Help identify opportunities to improve the efficiency, consistency and quality of the Athletics Communications operation. Assist with special projects and department-wide communications initiatives as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: ●\tStrong writing, editing and communication skills. ●\tAbility to produce accurate, timely content in a fast-paced environment. ●\tStrong attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. ●\tAbility to gather information through interviews, research and event observation. ●\tAbility to work independently while also collaborating effectively with coaches, staff and student-athletes. ●\tStrong organizational and time-management skills. ●\tAbility to manage multiple assignments and deadlines. ●\tFamiliarity with social media platforms and digital content creation. ●\tWillingness to work evenings, weekends and athletic events as required. Preferred Qualifications: ●\tExperience covering collegiate athletics. ●\tExperience writing game stories, recaps, previews or feature stories. ●\tExperience with live social media coverage of sporting events. ●\tFamiliarity with athletics statistics, game management or sports information systems. ●\tExperience with photography, videography or other digital content creation. ●\tFamiliarity with AP style and sports writing conventions. ●\tEnrollment in or completion of a degree program in communications, journalism, public relations, sports management, marketing or a related field. Physical Demands: Talking : Frequently Hearing : Frequently Working Conditions: Extreme cold : Occasionally Extreme heat : Occasionally Humid : Occasionally Wet : Occasionally Noise : Frequently Temperature Change : Occasionally Employment Policies and other information: The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic information, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment . As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility . This position is not eligible for benefits. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State Universities Retirement System You do not pay Social Security taxes and your earnings will not be on your Social Security record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages.) Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse ***Please Note: All postings close at 5:00pm CST on the posting close date.*** Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"
