    "https://uis.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/1345?c=uis": {
      "title": "Extra Help Assistant Producer for Athletics Streaming",
      "description": "Extra Help Assistant Producer for Athletics Streaming | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) English (UK) Extra Help Assistant Producer for Athletics Streaming Springfield, IL, United States | 1005201 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/21/2026 Back to Search Extra Help Assistant Producer for Athletics Streaming Posting Category: About UIS: Located in the state capital, the University of Illinois Springfield is one of three members of the University of Illinois system. The University serves more than 4,000 students in 44 graduate and 56 undergraduate programs. You are encouraged to visit the university web page at http://www.uis.edu . Application deadline: 11/4/2026 Minimum Starting Salary: $20 per hour Job Summary: The Athletics Streaming Quality Coordinator serves as the primary liaison between UIS Athletics and the Office of Electronic Media to support, evaluate and continuously improve the quality, consistency and compliance of the department's live athletic broadcasts. Working within Athletics, this position will monitor and review live streams, assess production quality, identify operational and technical issues, and develop and implement improvements to streaming practices. The coordinator will ensure broadcasts meet applicable Great Lakes Valley Conference (GLVC) Sports Network requirements and NCAA postseason streaming standards. The position will also provide hands-on production support when needed, including camera operation, b-roll collection and assistance during periods of limited staffing or special events. The successful candidate will be proactive, detail-oriented and committed to ongoing evaluation. The position is intended to serve as a bridge between Athletics and the staff within OEM responsible for producing and operating live streams, helping establish clear expectations, improve communication and create a more consistent viewing experience for Prairie Stars audiences. Duties & Responsibilities: Streaming Evaluation and Quality Assurance - Regularly review live athletic streams and recorded broadcasts to assess picture quality, audio quality, camera work, graphics, commentary, replays, production consistency and overall viewer experience. Conduct pre-event, in-event and post-event quality checks to identify technical, operational, production and compliance concerns. Evaluate broadcasts against applicable GLVC Sports Network requirements and NCAA postseason streaming standards. Maintain records of evaluations, identified issues and areas requiring attention. Prepare written evaluations and communicate findings to Athletics and Office of Electronic Media staff. Identify recurring issues and determine their potential impact on broadcast quality, reliability, accessibility and compliance. Planning and Continuous Improvement - Work with Athletics and the Office of Electronic Media to develop and implement solutions based on streaming evaluations. Establish priorities for addressing immediate concerns and improving broadcast operations on an ongoing basis. Develop and maintain procedures, checklists and standards that support consistent, high-quality broadcasts. Recommend improvements to staffing, equipment use, camera placement, production workflows, communication and training. Assist with implementing changes and monitor their effectiveness through subsequent evaluations. Help prepare and update streaming plans for regular-season, special-event and NCAA postseason broadcasts. Support the development of training materials and procedures for student workers and other stream personnel. Streaming Compliance - Review applicable GLVC Sports Network streaming requirements and ensure UIS broadcasts are planned and produced in accordance with conference expectations. Monitor NCAA postseason streaming requirements and assist Athletics and Office of Electronic Media staff in preparing to meet applicable standards for postseason events. Maintain current knowledge of GLVC, NCAA and platform-specific streaming requirements. Assist with documenting compliance procedures and developing repeatable processes for regular-season and postseason broadcasts. Event and Production Support - Assist with live event production during periods of limited staffing, high-volume competition or special events. Operate a camera or other production equipment as needed and within the employee’s training and qualifications. Collect b-roll and other video content to support athletic broadcasts, digital content and promotional needs. Assist with pre-event setup, testing and post-event responsibilities when necessary. Provide additional production support for special events, postseason competition and other high-priority broadcasts. Perform other duties as assigned in support of UIS Athletics communications, operations and streaming initiatives. Minimum Qualifications: ●\tKnowledge of live sports streaming, video production or broadcast operations. ●\tStrong understanding of video and audio quality standards. ●\tAbility to evaluate broadcasts objectively and identify specific areas for improvement. ●\tKnowledge of or ability to learn GLVC Sports Network and NCAA streaming requirements. ●\tStrong organizational skills and attention to detail. ●\tAbility to document findings, track issues and follow through on corrective actions. ●\tStrong written and verbal communication skills. ●\tAbility to work collaboratively with technical and nontechnical staff. ●\tAbility to prioritize tasks and respond effectively to time-sensitive issues. ●\tWillingness to work evenings, weekends and special events as required by the athletics schedule. ●\tAbility to operate video production equipment or learn to do so with appropriate training. Preferred Qualifications: ●\tExperience with live sports streaming, television production, video production or broadcast operations. ●\tExperience with athletic event production. ●\tFamiliarity with streaming platforms, production software, cameras, audio equipment and broadcast graphics. ●\tExperience conducting quality assurance reviews or developing operational procedures. ●\tKnowledge of NCAA Division II athletics and conference streaming requirements. ●\tExperience working with student employees or training production personnel. Physical Demands: Talking : Frequently Hearing : Frequently Working Conditions: Extreme cold : Occasionally Extreme heat : Occasionally Humid : Occasionally Wet : Occasionally Noise : Frequently Temperature Change : Occasionally Employment Policies and other information: The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, and diversity. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment and we welcome applications from qualified individuals of all backgrounds and identities. The University of Illinois System does not discriminate against any applicant or employee based on their real or perceived race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, age, order of protection status, genetic information, marital status, disability, sexual orientation including gender identity, unfavorable discharge from the military or status as a protected veteran and will comply with all federal and state nondiscrimination, equal opportunity and affirmative action laws, orders and regulations. Visit University of Illinois Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Illinois System conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment. Convictions are not a bar to employment. Background checks will be performed in compliance with state and federal law. The University of Illinois System requires candidates selected for hire to disclose any documented finding of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment and to authorize inquiries to current and former employers regarding findings of sexual misconduct or sexual harassment. For more information, visit Policy on Consideration of Sexual Misconduct in Prior Employment . As a qualifying federal contractor, the University of Illinois System uses E-Verify to verify employment eligibility . This position is not eligible for benefits. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position, however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. UIS employment in this role is not covered by Social Security, and instead, is covered by the State Universities Retirement System You do not pay Social Security taxes and your earnings will not be on your Social Security record. (Your record will, however, show your Medicare wages.) Your pension from the State Universities Retirement System may affect the amount of your: Social Security benefit and Social Security benefit as a spouse ***Please Note: All postings close at 5:00pm CST on the posting close date.*** Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, COVID-19 vaccination requirement, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify. University of Illinois at Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The University of Illinois Springfield Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available. This report includes statistics from the previous three years concerning reported crime that occurred on campus, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by the University of Illinois Springfield campus and statistics for fires in on-campus student housing. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security and other safety information along with fire safety policies and procedures. To access the report online: http://www.uis.edu/about/overview/safety/ To obtain a hard copy: University Police Department, University of Illinois Springfield, One University Plaza, MS PDB1, Springfield, IL 62703-5407 University of Illinois at Springfield . One University Plaza . MS HRB30 . Springfield, Illinois 62703 . 217-206-6652. www.uis.edu/humanresources"
